1. OpenAvatarChat (fork base)
   https://github.com/HumanAIGC-Engineering/OpenAvatarChat
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Pinned commit: 8b7b3b4 (v0.6.0)
   This repository forks OpenAvatarChat and specializes it for
   SoulX-FlashHead real-time WebRTC avatars. The chat engine, handler
   framework, RTC transport, and WebUI are derived from OpenAvatarChat.

2. SoulX-FlashHead (vendored inference engine)
   https://github.com/Soul-AILab/SoulX-FlashHead
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Vendored commit: c2b0b0f (flash_head/ package byte-identical; the
   upstream commit is c2b0b0f, matched by 9bc03de for flash_head files)
   Location: src/handlers/avatar/flashhead/SoulX-FlashHead/
   Local modifications:
     - flash_head/configs/infer_params.yaml: sample_shift tuned 5 -> 8
       for more stable eye motion.
     - flash_head/utils/cpu_face_handler.py: mediapipe import made lazy
       so use_face_crop=false works without mediapipe installed.
   See scripts/refresh_flashhead.sh for how to refresh this vendored copy.

3. silero-vad (vendored VAD)
   https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad
   License: MIT
   Vendored: the silero_vad python package (src/ + LICENSE) with the
   pre-downloaded ONNX/JIT models under src/silero_vad/data/.

4. OpenAvatarChat-WebUI (vendored built frontend)
   https://github.com/HumanAIGC-Engineering/OpenAvatarChat-WebUI
   License: Apache License 2.0
   Vendored: the built dist/ directory (source of record for the build
   lives upstream). Local modifications: mobile-first CSS layout fixes
   applied to dist/assets/main.BHFa5GgP.css.

5. Smart Turn EOU / pipecat-ai (model download only)
   https://github.com/pipecat-ai/smart-turn
   The duplex (end-of-utterance) mode downloads the smart-turn-v3 ONNX
   model via scripts/download_smart_turn_weights.sh. The handler does
   not vendor or import the upstream package at runtime.

